Z||000003||stimpy||06-01-2001||06:17 PM||||Well, it's out of stock, so maybe ya won't be getting it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I had a Sanyo deck once, a looong time ago. It was a cheap piece o' crap, but it was the lowest model in their line-up, so that's no surprise.  Without knowing too much about this unit, I still think you would be happier scraping together another yard and getting a Pioneer DEH-P77DH from <A HREF="http://www.competitionsound.com" TARGET=_blank>www.competitionsound.com</A>  <BR>It has 3 sets of preamp outputs (F,R,& sub), remote, built-in alarm, and built-in 180w MOSFET power supply. Definately a cool unit.<BR>The one thing I'd say about that Sanyo that I don't like is the knob on the right side, I don't like reaching that far over to control any functions. The Pioneer has everything on the left. Also has never ever skipped on me on Oklahoma (potholes) roads.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||06-01-2001||07:27 PM||||The unit looks good but I'm with Stimpy on this, Get the Pioneer. It's a much better unit with more functions and more power.<P>On the specials from Crutchfield, Every time I see a special or get a special sales flyer, most of the "great deal" items are "out of stock" Last year they had a set of JBL  top of the line 4" seperates that were retail listed for $450.00 and Crutchfield had a close-out sale of $129.95 a set. I called an hour after getting the flyer in the  mail and they were sold out.   <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric||06-01-2001||07:54 PM||||Crutchfield wants $80 more than Competition Sound for the reciever Stimpy is talking about.<P>What's the advantage of the p77 over the p47?||||reg||1
Z||000006||SPDFREK||06-01-2001||08:19 PM||||Best buy had these head units on sale about 2 weeks ago, if I could find my receipt I would tell you the full price, I think I paid like $200 for the head unit.( I bought amps and boxes and speakers at the same time, so not real sure.) but it works Great, 3 pre outs. sub,front,rear, 4 channel wires, electronic sub control, high & low pass filters, remote, detachable face, mini disk and compact disk cap. and has a remote connection for a mp3 player or disk changer.<P>     <IMG SRC="http://home.talkcity.com/ArcadeAlley/jkolley/headunit1.gif">     <P>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker<P>PS, I have to right click, and click show pic for it to show, you might have to too. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by SPDFREK (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||06-01-2001||08:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric:<BR><B>Crutchfield wants $80 more than Competition Sound for the reciever Stimpy is talking about.<P>What's the advantage of the p77 over the p47?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The P77 has the built-in car alarm, a remote, and the subwoofer control and outputs.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||06-01-2001||08:59 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>The unit looks good but I'm with Stimpy on this, Get the Pioneer. It's a much better unit with more functions and more power.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree completely. <BR>I'm sure you get what you pay for. Just that 1.5 DIN units are so uncommon, I thought I'd pass it along. <BR>I sure wish Kenwood would make one.<P>I have a P77, that I'm going to install in my Sonoma when I get the time. The system that's in there now is getting raggedy, like the rest of the truck.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Was going to put it in the Fiero, but found a Pontiac CD player, instead. <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||1
